{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>A widow and a divorcée.</b> From this alien man." "<b>And has no seed.</b> From him." "<b>And returns.</b> This teaches: if she has seed from him, she is forbidden in terumah as long as the seed is alive (Yevamot 77)." "<b>And any alien shall not eat of it.</b> It comes only to exclude the onen — who is permitted in terumah; I say to you 'alienness,' but not onen-status (ibid. 68)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:43.375282817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}